      "message": "**Missing barrier before the CWRITER doorbell.** Between the `memcpy()` of the command bytes into the hyp command queue and the `writeq_relaxed()` to `GITS_CWRITER` that rings the doorbell, there\u0027s no `dsb(ishst)`. The ITS may observe the doorbell before the command bytes are visible in memory. Please add `dsb(ishst)` after the memcpy and before the doorbell write. \n\nSeparately: the command queue\u0027s cacheability comes from GITS_CBASER InnerCache/OuterCache, so if it\u0027s programmed non-cacheable this needs cache maintenance, not only a barrier. Worth confirming which side owns that.",
